  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<b>9 \xB7 The course's global settings</b>\n<size=70%>These settings belong to the project, not to a scene or a package. The course sets them once. Each line gives where the setting is and why.\n\n<b>The URP Asset (Assets/Settings/PC_RPAsset)</b>\n- Quality > HDR: on. Bloom and tonemapping need values above 1.\n- Quality > Anti Aliasing (MSAA): 4x. Thin edges stay smooth when the camera moves.\n- Post-processing > Grading Mode: High Dynamic Range. The grade works on the full range, before tonemapping.\n- Rendering > Depth Texture and Opaque Texture: on. Glass, water and soft particles read them.\n- Shadows > Max Distance: 50 m. Beyond it, nothing casts a shadow.\n- Volumes > Volume Profile: None. No hidden post-processing under every scene.\n\n<b>The Renderer (Assets/Settings/PC_Renderer)</b>\n- Rendering Path: Forward+.\n- Renderer Features: Decal (DBuffer, Use Rendering Layers on), Screen Space Ambient Occlusion, Screen Space Reflection, Volumetric Fog. Each adds a pass to every frame.\n\n<b>The project (Edit > Project Settings)</b>\n- Graphics > Default Render Pipeline: PC_RPAsset. Used when a Quality level names no asset.\n- Graphics > Volume > Default Profile: Screen Space Reflection set to Disabled. A scene turns it on in its own Volume.\n- Quality > the PC level's Render Pipeline Asset: PC_RPAsset.\n- Player > Other Settings > Color Space: Linear.\n- Player > Other Settings > Scripting Define Symbols: URP_SCREEN_SPACE_REFLECTION. Without it the Screen Space Reflection feature does nothing.\n- Tags and Layers > User Layers 8-11: Post-Tonemapping, Post-Bloom, Post-Grading, Post-Vignette-Grain (the Post-Processing scene).</size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2100000, guid: f2e792e711a8fb24fb0c2ed977107618, type: 2}
