  m_text: 'This project computes light in Linear colour space (Edit > Project Settings > Player > Other Settings > Color Space), the setting correct lighting needs; Gamma is the older setting. The colour picker shows gamma-encoded (sRGB) values: the numbers are not the share of light a surface reflects.


    <b>Predict:</b> Swatch A is set to 0.1, 0.1, 0.1 in the colour picker. Does it reflect a tenth of the light, or much less?


    <b>Try:</b>

    1. Select Swatch A and open its Base Map colour picker. Read the values.

    2. Compare swatches 0, A, B and C side by side.

    3. Read Color Space in the Player settings. Leave it on Linear.


    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Material-Chart (the reference values)</color></size>'
