  m_text: "Without anti-aliasing each pixel takes the colour of one point: inside an object or outside it. Thin edges turn into staircases. Anti-aliasing smooths them: MSAA in the URP Asset (Quality > Anti Aliasing (MSAA)), or FXAA, SMAA or TAA on each camera (Rendering > Anti-aliasing).\n\n<b>Predict:</b> MSAA is set to 4x here. You set it to Disabled while the camera drifts slowly past the far railing. What do the railing's thin bars do?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Look through Camera - 7 and press Play.\n2. Set PC_RPAsset > Quality > Anti Aliasing (MSAA) to Disabled and watch the railing. Set it back to 4x.\n3. Stop Play.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: 9 \xB7 The course's global settings</color></size>"
