  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "A render pipeline is the program that draws each frame: which objects, in what order, with which lights. Unity has three: the Built-in Render Pipeline, URP and HDRP. This project uses URP. A shader is written for one render pipeline, so a material made for another pipeline does not work here.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> These three materials use the Built-in pipeline's Standard shader. What colour will URP draw them?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Select the Crate and read the Shader at the top of its material.\n2. Open Edit > Project Settings > Graphics and read Default Render Pipeline.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Shaders-Training, 4 \xB7 Magenta \xB7 the exercise Fix-The-Pink</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
